From c8d126451f850d5add69b910cfa76628b97d4fe6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Bryniarski <michael.bryniarski@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:01:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] dndcp: add native Wayland drag and drop

On a Wayland session, DnDUIX11 drags through Xwayland, and KWin does not
carry those drags between X11 and Wayland clients for vmware-user:
host-to-guest drops never complete, and guest drags never reach the
detection window.

DnDUIWayland handles the common DnD layer's signals with Wayland
protocols instead:

- The detection window is the input region of a transparent
  wlr-layer-shell overlay covering the output (a 1x1 buffer stretched by
  wp_viewporter). The surface never moves; its input region is in effect
  as soon as the commit is processed, unlike a layer surface's position.
- Host to guest: a uinput press on the detection window gives the serial
  that starts a wl_data_device drag offering the host's file list, text
  or RTF, copy only.
- Guest to host: on DND_CMD_QUERY_EXITING the uinput button is held down,
  so compositors that pass on a release only once no device on the seat
  holds a button (KWin) keep the guest drag alive while the pointer is
  moved onto the detection window, where the drag's data is read for the
  host.

A file list from the host is refused as a whole if any name is unsafe
(see WaylandUtil_IsSafeRelativePath), resetting the drag.

CopyPasteDnDX11 holds the DnD UI through a small DnDUI interface and
uses DnDUIWayland when the session is Wayland and the compositor offers
layer-shell, wl_data_device_manager v3 and wp_viewporter, and DnDUIX11
otherwise (e.g. GNOME). VMTOOLS_DND_BACKEND=x11|wayland forces either.

Guest-to-host drags still fail when DND_CMD_QUERY_EXITING reaches the
guest after the host's button release, which RpcIn's polling backoff (up
to 100ms) makes common. Host file contents (Windows hosts) are not
handled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
